  'pieter-coetze-world-record-backstroke-2026-10-15',
  'Pretoria swimmer Pieter Coetzé sets world record, wins again',
  'Sport', '2026-10-15', 'TimesLIVE', 'https://www.timeslive.co.za/sport/2026-10-15-pieter-coetze-wins-again-in-kazakhstan-to-move-up-rankings/',
  'Pretoria''s Pieter Coetzé broke a short-course world record in Uzbekistan this month and then won again in Kazakhstan.',
  'Pretoria-born swimmer Pieter Coetzé set his first career world record on 9 October, clocking 22.09 seconds in the short-course men''s 50m backstroke at a Swimming World Cup meet in Tashkent, Uzbekistan. The swim lowered the previous global mark of 22.11, held by Russia''s Kliment Kolesnikov since 2022, and improved on Coetzé''s own personal best of 22.51, set only days earlier.

At the World Cup series'' final stop in Astana, Kazakhstan, Coetzé went on to win the men''s 100m backstroke in 48.40 seconds, taking that event for a third straight leg of the series. The swim ranked as the fourth-fastest 100m backstroke ever recorded in a short-course pool, behind the world record of 48.16 held by Hungary''s Hubert Kos.

With two rounds of the series left to swim, Coetzé sat on 134.1 points in the men''s overall World Cup standings, just behind Russia''s Egor Kornev, the series leader on 134.4. Coetzé said the new record had been on his mind, but that it would not change his approach, adding: "you can never get too comfortable."',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
  '["https://www.timeslive.co.za/sport/2026-10-15-pieter-coetze-wins-again-in-kazakhstan-to-move-up-rankings/", "https://www.citizen.co.za/rekord/sports-news/local-sports/2026/10/12/coetze-breaks-world-record-at-swimming-world-cup-in-uzbekistan/"]',
  'agent'
);
